4 #edb/ref 17592186288557 13194139534443 true] [17592186288552 1110 #uuid "3906e258-840c-5de5-af0e-44d141899def" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288553 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288553 1111 #uuid "a47b88ad-e6a3-548e-b3a7-95ede04a074e" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288554 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288554 1111 #uuid "28e902a6-5051-5cca-b30e-0fee2f148317" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288555 1034 "-\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288555 1111 #uuid "b5b15967-d3ef-551a-947f-bfb28904e4a9" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288556 1034 "4" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288556 1111 #uuid "debcc437-3577-57c9-b607-c2c9c289e770" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288557 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288557 1111 #uuid "4e80adb5-d2d0-5375-ac8e-96c908f4c86d" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288559 13194139534443 true] [17592186288558 1089 "q-275755" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534443 true] [17592186288558 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288558 1113 #uuid "7fedf1ce-1d8a-575c-bbd4-9093e6ecd764" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288558 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2+2)-0-3(2-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(6-0) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288560 13194139534443 true] [17592186288559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288561 13194139534443 true] [17592186288559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534443 true] [17592186288559 1041 "field-1" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288561 13194139534443 true] [17592186288559 1110 #uuid "197b5c36-1e0b-5239-8e5a-8e1d24c83ee2" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288560 1034 "1" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288560 1111 #uuid "ee3e2b62-ecd3-52a1-9ef1-f87f4614c55c" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288561 1034 "-1" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288561 1111 #uuid "43a3fbd2-7f9b-5efe-b807-f44b9545e81a" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288562 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288563 13194139534443 true] [17592186288562 1089 "q-319413" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288562 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534443 true] [17592186288562 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288562 1113 #uuid "bfe6bc14-6591-5f71-bb33-e7e4cf7f033e" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288562 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288564 13194139534443 true] [17592186288563 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534443 true] [17592186288563 1041 "field-1" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288563 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288564 13194139534443 true] [17592186288563 1110 #uuid "2fb06bcc-74a6-5677-a4f1-bd2028bab163" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288564 1034 "-\\frac{1}{11}" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288564 1111 #uuid "55b1616d-08df-5ad7-ba02-103428efcd35" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288566 13194139534443 true] [17592186288565 1089 "q-73542" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534443 true] [17592186288565 1100 "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $1.$ Find the value of $k.$" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288565 1113 #uuid "f2b1695b-282d-54b6-9ac9-0c3ba20a588b" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288565 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288567 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288568 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288569 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288570 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288571 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1041 "selection" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288569 13194139534443 true] [17592186288566 1110 #uuid "c8b32d26-4ce1-5e64-80c3-4102cfcaad63" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288567 1034 "3" 13194139534443 true] [17592186288567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534443 true] [17592186288567 1111 #uuid "0cfddfff-2